## All-metal detail, without enamel

Die-struck pins express your design through raised metal and recessed backgrounds rather than enamel color. Sandblasted recesses contrast with polished highlights, giving lettering, crests and emblems a clear, understated finish for uniforms, corporate recognition and commemorative editions.

## From artwork to finished pin

The approved artwork defines the outline, lettering and relief before a custom die is cut. The design is struck into metal, finished with the selected surface texture and plating, and assembled with the chosen backing. Gold, nickel and antique finishes create different levels of contrast without adding color fill.

Keep fine lettering readable at the actual pin size. Strong outlines and controlled recesses preserve the character of the emblem; a polished border can frame a textured background without competing with the main design.

## Choose the presentation to suit the occasion

- Corporate and employee recognition: a restrained metal finish for logos and service milestones.
- Military, government and association insignia: clear crests, mottos and formal borders.
- Commemorative and fundraising programs: dates and symbols coordinated with a backing card or gift box.

## Plan your order

The minimum order is 50 pieces. Typical production takes 7-15 business days, excluding shipping; the final schedule is confirmed with the artwork and quotation. Send your logo or sketch, intended size, quantity, delivery country and target date. Backing and packaging choices can be refined during the design review.
